e air\n\n1186\n01:07:29,254 --> 01:07:33,049\nbut enabled them\nto draw oxygen from the sea.\n\n1187\n01:07:36,386 --> 01:07:38,137\nThey settled in the ocean,\n\n1188\n01:07:38,805 --> 01:07:41,933\naway from war and diseases.\n\n1189\n01:07:44,519 --> 01:07:45,603\n(SHAMAN SPEAKING MAYAN)\n\n1190\n01:07:45,687 --> 01:07:46,729\n(SHAMAN GRUNTS)\n\n1191\n01:07:50,024 --> 01:07:52,068\n(EERIE MUSIC CONTINUES)\n\n1192\n01:07:58,366 --> 01:08:00,785\n(WOMAN WHISPERING BLESSING\nIN SPANISH)\n\n1193\n01:08:01,703 --> 01:08:03,121\n(RITUALISTIC RHYTHMIC BLOWING)\n\n1194\n01:08:11,087 --> 01:08:13,256\n(IN ENGLISH) My mother\ngave birth to me there\n\n1195\n01:08:13,548 --> 01:08:16,801\nand I became\nthe firstborn son of Talokan.\n\n1196\n01:08:17,260 --> 01:08:19,345\nThe plant gave me wings\non my ankles\n\n1197\n01:08:19,512 --> 01:08:21,931\nand ears\nthat pointed to the clouds.\n\n1198\n01:08:22,390 --> 01:08:23,641\nI was a mutant.\n\n1199\n01:08:24,559 --> 01:08:27,812\nI could swim in the sky\nand age slower.\n\n1200\n01:08:27,979 --> 01:08:30,481\nBreathe the air\nour ancestors breathed.\n\n1201\n01:08:31,733 --> 01:08:33,318\nAs she grew older,\n\n1202\n01:08:34,652 --> 01:08:38,239\nmy mother mourned the life\non land that she once knew...\n\n1203\n01:08:40,158 --> 01:08:41,909\nand died with a broken heart.\n\n1204\n01:08:44,662 --> 01:08:46,289\nShe made me promise\n\n1205\n01:08:46,372 --> 01:08:48,625\nto bury her\nin the soil of her homeland.\n\n1206\n01:08:53,755 --> 01:08:56,674\nNothing could prepare me\nfor what I found there.\n\n1207\n01:08:56,758 --> 01:08:58,551\n-(MEN SHOUTING)\n-(WHIPS LASHING)\n\n1208\n01:08:58,635 --> 01:09:00,345\n(SLAVES GROANING)\n\n1209\n01:09:00,428 --> 01:09:02,055\n-(MAN SHOUTS IN SPANISH)\n-(WOMAN GROANS)\n\n1210\n01:09:04,057 --> 01:09:05,141\n(IN SPANISH)\n\n1211\n01:09:06,309 --> 01:09:07,310\nHuh?\n\n1212\n01:09:07,935 --> 01:09:10,104\n(EERIE MUSIC PLAYING)\n\n1213\n01:09:18,446 --> 01:09:20,281\n(MUSIC SOURS)\n\n12